      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2015-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(625 = 5^4,\\) we have \\[ \\begin{gathered} 625^{\\log_5 2015} = 5^{4\\log_5 2015} \\\\ = \\left(5^{\\log_5 2015}\\right)^4 = 2015^4. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nTaking the fourth root gives \\(\\left(2015^4\\right)^{\\frac{1}{4}} = 2015.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
